---
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_EDITORIAL_TEAM } from '../lib/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title={`Editorial method & corrections — ${SITE_NAME}`} description={`How ${SITE_NAME} researches destinations, checks sources, credits images and handles corrections.`} path="/editorial-policy/">
  <section class="container section-block">
    <div class="page-intro"><h1>Editorial policy</h1></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Official sources</h2>
      <p>We use the organization responsible for the information, such as a park service for closures, an attraction for booking rules, or a transit operator for ticket coverage. Guides identify their sources and the date of the relevant check. We hold information when a source is unavailable or the evidence conflicts.</p>
      <h2>Research and experience</h2>
      <p>Our destination recommendations and guides are based on research by the {SITE_EDITORIAL_TEAM}. We identify firsthand visits when a real contributor reports one.</p>
      <h2>Use of automated tools</h2>
      <p>We use AI tools to organize source material and draft articles. The first five releases received approval for their exact text. New releases must pass automated checks for source freshness, factual coverage, duplicate content and publication limits. Official references let readers check the evidence directly.</p>
      <h2>Changing information</h2>
      <p>Time-sensitive facts have a recheck date. The page points to the official source when a fact needs renewal or its evidence changes. Check the linked attraction or operator for current details before setting out.</p>
      <h2>Images and illustrations</h2>
      <p>Destination photos identify the place, creator and reuse license. Original artwork and AI illustrations are labeled, with details in <a href="/photo-credits/">Photo credits</a>. Use the official sources to check access, routes and facilities.</p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>Please <a href="/contact/">report a correction</a> with the page, disputed claim and an official reference where available. A material correction changes the article’s update date.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
